00:08:49.795 --> 00:08:52.565 align:start size:88% position:13%
then it's systemic risk,
whatever that means.

00:08:53.666 --> 00:08:55.400
Then the taxpayer is
gonna be on the hook.

00:08:55.400 --> 00:08:58.904
I am totally opposed to that
as to why this is happening.

00:08:58.904 --> 00:09:01.640 align:start size:84% position:16%
The big banks are
out there right now.

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:03.943 align:start size:97% position:3%
If you ask me and just talking
to people watching this,

00:09:03.943 --> 00:09:07.613 align:start size:97% position:3%
the big banks are out there
trying to drive down the stock

00:09:07.613 --> 00:09:09.949 align:start size:84% position:16%
and trying to drive
down the assets

00:09:09.949 --> 00:09:12.250 align:start size:84% position:16%
of these medium size
and smaller banks

00:09:12.250 --> 00:09:13.518
'cause they wanna
gobble 'em all up.

00:09:13.518 --> 00:09:15.187 align:start size:97% position:3%
And the Biden
administration's helping them,

00:09:15.187 --> 00:09:18.190
they're for that, because
the bigger the banks get,

00:09:18.190 --> 00:09:20.592
then the more the government
can partner with the big banks.

00:09:20.592 --> 00:09:22.461 align:start size:84% position:16%
And they want
three or four banks

00:09:22.461 --> 00:09:24.830 align:start size:97% position:3%
that will be basically
controlled by the government

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:26.866
because then they can debank

00:09:26.866 --> 00:09:29.702
and decredit people who don't
do what they're told to do,

00:09:29.702 --> 00:09:33.272 align:start size:97% position:3%
like gun owners and people who
sell guns, for one example.

00:09:33.272 --> 00:09:34.606
- Right, so we get
three or four banks,

00:09:34.606 --> 00:09:36.508 align:start size:88% position:13%
but in essence, we
really just get one bank

00:09:36.508 --> 00:09:38.477
because it's the United
States government saying.

00:09:38.477 --> 00:09:39.945
So what do we do about that?

00:09:39.945 --> 00:09:42.581
I mean, we keep hearing more
about this like global currency

00:09:42.581 --> 00:09:45.817 align:start position:0%
or there's gonna be this
United States digital currency.

00:09:45.817 --> 00:09:48.320
DeSantis is fighting hard
against it in Florida,

00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:50.122
it sounds like about
20 other red states

00:09:50.122 --> 00:09:52.357
are kind of joining him on that.

00:09:52.357 --> 00:09:53.625
Is it just inevitable

00:09:53.625 --> 00:09:56.028
that we'll all continue
to go in this direction?

00:09:56.028 --> 00:09:57.529
- Oh no, goodness sakes, no.

00:09:57.529 --> 00:09:59.097
No, it's not inevitable.

00:09:59.097 --> 00:10:00.365
We've gotta hit reverse.

00:10:00.365 --> 00:10:01.767
I mean, one of the
things I disagree

00:10:01.767 --> 00:10:04.737 align:start position:0%
with a lot of my fellow
Republicans in Washington about

00:10:04.737 --> 00:10:07.139 align:start size:88% position:13%
is that they've been
for this big bank stuff.

00:10:07.139 --> 00:10:09.708
I mean, they're the ones
who have put in place,

00:10:09.708 --> 00:10:12.244
or in some instances,
taken away the barriers

00:10:12.244 --> 00:10:13.545
for letting the big
banks get bigger.

00:10:13.545 --> 00:10:14.780
So what should we do?

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:15.982
I think we ought to
say to the big banks,

00:10:15.982 --> 00:10:17.416 align:start size:81% position:19%
"You can't get
any bigger, sorry,

00:10:17.416 --> 00:10:19.150
"you can't buy up anymore

00:10:19.150 --> 00:10:21.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
"of these small and medium
sized banks, no more."

00:10:21.086 --> 00:10:22.321
Number two, we're
not gonna bail,

00:10:22.321 --> 00:10:23.555
we're not gonna
sweeten this deal

00:10:23.555 --> 00:10:25.925 align:start size:81% position:19%
by bailing out all
of these banks,

00:10:25.925 --> 00:10:27.226
because who profits from that?

00:10:27.226 --> 00:10:30.329
What happens is the
big banks come in,

00:10:30.329 --> 00:10:32.197
they get the bailout
money essentially,

00:10:32.197 --> 00:10:33.733
and they gobble up
the little banks.

00:10:33.733 --> 00:10:35.568
So we're gonna stop that
whole sweetheart deal,

00:10:35.568 --> 00:10:37.336
no more of these
secret bailouts.

00:10:37.336 --> 00:10:39.538
We're not gonna let the
big banks get any bigger.

00:10:39.538 --> 00:10:41.207 align:start size:84% position:16%
And we're gonna play
put in place laws

00:10:41.207 --> 00:10:44.343 align:start size:97% position:3%
that actually help and protect
community banks like local,

00:10:44.343 --> 00:10:46.012
truly local banks,

00:10:46.012 --> 00:10:47.780
where people know each other

00:10:47.780 --> 00:10:50.683 align:start size:97% position:3%
and you can go get a loan
from somebody who knows you,

00:10:50.683 --> 00:10:52.885 align:start size:88% position:13%
and it's not being
controlled and dictated

00:10:52.885 --> 00:10:54.754
by Washington or Wall Street.

00:10:54.754 --> 00:10:56.722
- Makes sense to
me, we shall see.

00:10:56.722 --> 00:10:58.290 align:start size:97% position:3%
All right, let's talk
about the book a little bit

00:10:58.290 --> 00:11:00.825 align:start size:88% position:13%
'cause I was flipping
through it this morning,

00:11:00.825 --> 00:11:03.462 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you're channeling your
inner Jordan Peterson,

00:11:03.462 --> 00:11:04.597
if I'm not mistaken.

00:11:05.664 --> 00:11:07.132 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Well, I think
that Jordan Peterson

00:11:07.132 --> 00:11:10.236
has been a powerful
and much needed voice

00:11:10.236 --> 00:11:13.005 align:start size:97% position:3%
in encouraging men all
around the world in his case,

00:11:13.005 --> 00:11:14.973 align:start size:88% position:13%
but men in this country
need to hear it,

00:11:14.973 --> 00:11:18.010 align:start size:84% position:16%
to say to them,
"Listen, we need you,

00:11:18.010 --> 00:11:20.412
"you are needed,
you are important.

00:11:20.412 --> 00:11:23.048
"You can be a force for good
and we need you to step up.

00:11:23.048 --> 00:11:25.818
"So turn off the computer
in mom and dad's basement,

00:11:25.818 --> 00:11:28.421
"come on out, go get a job,

00:11:28.421 --> 00:11:30.856
"maybe get married,
start a family."

00:11:30.856 --> 00:11:32.624
That is how you're
gonna leave a legacy.

00:11:32.624 --> 00:11:34.760
That is how you can
change this country.

00:11:34.760 --> 00:11:36.294 align:start size:84% position:16%
And really the
book is about that.

00:11:36.294 --> 00:11:38.730
It's about how we need men
to be all that they can be

00:11:38.730 --> 00:11:41.734
so that America can
be all that we can.

00:11:41.734 --> 00:11:44.437
- Are you surprised that you
had to write a book like this?

00:11:44.437 --> 00:11:46.172
I've heard you talk
about this before,

00:11:46.172 --> 00:11:48.374
the issue about men in society,

00:11:48.374 --> 00:11:50.342
but look, you're a senator.

00:11:50.342 --> 00:11:51.610
Mostly people would think,

00:11:51.610 --> 00:11:52.912
"Oh, he's gonna write
a book about politics,"

00:11:52.912 --> 00:11:54.613
but that's really
not what this is.

00:11:54.613 --> 00:11:56.982
- No, yeah, it's
not about politics.

00:11:56.982 --> 00:12:00.452 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I suppose it is surprising
given just where we are.

00:12:00.452 --> 00:12:02.121
I'm surprised at the
message to the left,

00:12:02.121 --> 00:12:05.891
I'm surprised at the
left's message to men,

00:12:05.891 --> 00:12:08.494
which is that manhood
is inherently toxic,

00:12:08.494 --> 00:12:10.830
they love this phrase,
"Toxic masculinity."

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:12.064
But if you listen closely,

00:12:12.064 --> 00:12:13.565
and I quote this
stuff in the book,

00:12:13.565 --> 00:12:15.768
if you listen closely to
what the leftists believe,

00:12:15.768 --> 00:12:18.137
they think all manhood is toxic.

00:12:18.137 --> 00:12:19.905
There's one social
scientist who said,

00:12:19.905 --> 00:12:22.107 align:start size:84% position:16%
"Talking about
healthy masculinity

00:12:22.107 --> 00:12:24.543 align:start size:84% position:16%
"is like talking
about healthy cancer."

00:12:24.543 --> 00:12:26.278 align:start size:84% position:16%
There you go, that's
the less view.

00:12:26.278 --> 00:12:27.513
And they tell our kids this,

00:12:27.513 --> 00:12:30.149 align:start size:88% position:13%
I've got two little
boys who are school age,

00:12:30.149 --> 00:12:32.284
I worry about what are
they hearing in school,

00:12:32.284 --> 00:12:33.552 align:start size:84% position:16%
what are they hearing
from the media.

00:12:33.552 --> 00:12:35.287
This is really the big
reason I wrote the book,

00:12:35.287 --> 00:12:36.522 align:start size:81% position:19%
I was thinking
about my own boys.

00:12:36.522 --> 00:12:38.657
Our boys, from the
time they're small,

00:12:38.657 --> 00:12:41.093
are told that being
a man is a problem,

00:12:41.093 --> 00:12:43.562 align:start size:84% position:16%
that men, when
they are masculine,

00:12:43.562 --> 00:12:46.565 align:start size:94% position:6%
hurt things, break things,
make society worse.

00:12:46.565 --> 00:12:48.701 align:start size:88% position:13%
We need to send the
exact opposite message,

00:12:48.701 --> 00:12:50.269
that we need strong men,

00:12:50.269 --> 00:12:52.304 align:start size:84% position:16%
we need you to
stand up and provide

00:12:52.304 --> 00:12:53.973
and protect and sacrifice,

00:12:53.973 --> 00:12:56.075
and you can change your family,

00:12:56.075 --> 00:12:58.010 align:start size:81% position:19%
you can change
your neighborhood,

00:12:58.010 --> 00:13:00.312 align:start size:97% position:3%
you can change your
country, if you'll do that.

00:13:00.312 --> 00:13:02.114
- We play the videos on my
show every now and again.

00:13:02.114 --> 00:13:04.249 align:start size:88% position:13%
But if you wanna see how
toxic masculinity is,

00:13:04.249 --> 00:13:07.920 align:start position:0%
go watch the videos from 1920's
New York City, Manhattan,

00:13:07.920 --> 00:13:10.588
when they have these guys
up on those skyscrapers,

00:13:10.588 --> 00:13:13.325 align:start size:97% position:3%
not strapped into anything,
hanging off there,

00:13:13.325 --> 00:13:16.595 align:start position:0%
building the Empire State
Building, absolutely incredible.

00:13:16.595 --> 00:13:18.430 align:start size:81% position:19%
What was really
the genesis of it?

00:13:18.430 --> 00:13:20.099
Was it really looking
at your kids and going,

00:13:20.099 --> 00:13:22.300
"They need a message on this."

00:13:22.300 --> 00:13:24.136 align:start size:94% position:6%
Where do you think we
really went off the rails

00:13:24.136 --> 00:13:25.037
on this thing?

00:13:26.405 --> 00:13:27.906
- Well, I think, in terms
of why I wrote the book,

00:13:27.906 --> 00:13:30.108
yeah, I've got a 10-year-old
and an 8-year-old, both boys.

00:13:30.108 --> 00:13:32.210
And then I've got a baby
girl, who's my youngest.

00:13:32.210 --> 00:13:35.047
But as my boys now get
older, really for me,

00:13:35.047 --> 00:13:36.515 align:start size:84% position:16%
the book started with
me thinking about

00:13:36.515 --> 00:13:38.950
what's my obligation as a dad

00:13:38.950 --> 00:13:41.487
to help my boys be who
they were meant to be.

00:13:41.487 --> 00:13:43.054 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, what is it
that I'm teaching 'em?

00:13:43.054 --> 00:13:45.524
And I look at what the
culture is teaching them.

00:13:45.524 --> 00:13:48.127 align:start size:97% position:3%
I'm like, "Man, that is
frightening and it is wrong."

00:13:48.127 --> 00:13:49.594
And so the book really started

00:13:49.594 --> 00:13:51.863
about me thinking through
that with my own kids.

00:13:51.863 --> 00:13:54.667 align:start size:97% position:3%
And the book is really about
holding out role models.

00:13:54.667 --> 00:13:56.168
I talk a lot about
American history,

00:13:56.168 --> 00:13:57.670
I talk a lot about the Bible,

00:13:57.670 --> 00:13:59.205
role models of what to look like

00:13:59.205 --> 00:14:01.139
to be a strong man
and to be a good man

00:14:01.139 --> 00:14:03.175
and tell those stories
about being a husband,

00:14:03.175 --> 00:14:05.611
being a father, being a warrior,

00:14:05.611 --> 00:14:08.280
being a builder, being a
priest, and being a king.

00:14:08.280 --> 00:14:10.182
And each of those is
a chapter of the book.

00:14:10.182 --> 00:14:11.683
And it's really saying to men,

00:14:11.683 --> 00:14:13.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Hey, there's something
that for you to go after,"

00:14:13.785 --> 00:14:17.957
we need you to step up and be
a contributor in these ways.

00:14:17.957 --> 00:14:19.257
So that's how it started.

00:14:19.257 --> 00:14:20.626
How do we go wrong?

00:14:20.626 --> 00:14:22.294
I think it's really the left

00:14:22.294 --> 00:14:24.630 align:start size:84% position:16%
and their embrace
of this new Marxism,

00:14:24.630 --> 00:14:28.166
which says that manhood is
toxic, that manhood is evil,

00:14:28.166 --> 00:14:31.136
that American society
is systemically racist

00:14:31.136 --> 00:14:33.538
and oppressive and bigoted,
and men are the problem.

00:14:33.538 --> 00:14:35.273 align:start size:84% position:16%
And that's a message
men are told,

00:14:35.273 --> 00:14:38.611 align:start size:97% position:3%
especially boys are told from
the time they are little.

00:14:38.611 --> 00:14:39.545
And we've gotta counteract that

00:14:39.545 --> 00:14:41.480
'cause it is just dead wrong.

00:14:41.480 --> 00:14:44.349
- How much of that stuff
is leaking into your life,

00:14:44.349 --> 00:14:45.984
your constituent's
life in Missouri?

00:14:45.984 --> 00:14:47.719 align:start size:88% position:13%
I feel like people
think about this stuff,

00:14:47.719 --> 00:14:49.989
they're like, "All right, it's
happening in schools in Cali,

00:14:49.989 --> 00:14:51.256
"it's happening in New York,

00:14:51.256 --> 00:14:53.859
"but it's probably not
happening in Missouri."

00:14:53.859 --> 00:14:55.727
- Oh no, it's in the
curriculum everywhere.

00:14:55.727 --> 00:14:57.195
I mean, that's the
sad part about it

00:14:57.195 --> 00:14:59.798
is that it is in
school curriculum.

00:14:59.798 --> 00:15:01.399
Look at the data, don't
take my word for it,

00:15:01.399 --> 00:15:02.334
just look at the data,

00:15:02.334 --> 00:15:05.137
look how often boys, young boys,

00:15:05.137 --> 00:15:08.607
elementary age boys are
diagnosed with ADHD,

00:15:08.607 --> 00:15:11.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
versus girls, versus
other demographics, right?

00:15:11.109 --> 00:15:14.446 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, it is overwhelmingly,
boys have been medicated

00:15:14.446 --> 00:15:17.149 align:start size:94% position:6%
basically into submission
in our schools.

00:15:17.149 --> 00:15:19.017
We've had a constant mantra

00:15:19.017 --> 00:15:21.954 align:start size:97% position:3%
that boys shouldn't be
allowed to play aggressively,

00:15:21.954 --> 00:15:23.922 align:start size:84% position:16%
if they bring toy
soldiers to schools.

00:15:23.922 --> 00:15:25.357
There's something
wrong with them

00:15:25.357 --> 00:15:28.627 align:start position:0%
if they bring a toy gun to
school, that's an intervention.

00:15:28.627 --> 00:15:32.798 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's crazy, it starts
early, and it's everywhere.

00:15:32.798 --> 00:15:35.167
I have parents talk to me
from all over my state,

00:15:35.167 --> 00:15:37.336
all over the country,
come and say that,

00:15:37.336 --> 00:15:39.071
"I just heard this happen,

00:15:39.071 --> 00:15:41.406
"my kid brought a
G.I. Joe to school,

00:15:41.406 --> 00:15:43.442 align:start size:94% position:6%
"he was disciplined for
it," et cetera, et cetera.

00:15:43.442 --> 00:15:45.177
It is crazy, crazy stuff.

00:15:45.177 --> 00:15:47.513
What is the effect
of that society-wide,

00:15:47.513 --> 00:15:49.014
again, just look at the numbers.

00:15:49.014 --> 00:15:51.617
Record numbers of young men
suffering from depression,

00:15:51.617 --> 00:15:54.286
record numbers of young men
trying to commit suicide,

00:15:54.286 --> 00:15:55.754
record numbers of young men

00:15:55.754 --> 00:15:58.190 align:start size:88% position:13%
struggling with drug
abuse and alcohol abuse,

00:15:58.190 --> 00:16:00.793
and record numbers
of men not working.

00:16:01.894 --> 00:16:03.895 align:start size:84% position:16%
So if you like that
pattern, then I'd say,

00:16:03.895 --> 00:16:06.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Great, keep doing what
the left wants you to do."

00:16:06.065 --> 00:16:07.432
But for those of us who say,

00:16:07.432 --> 00:16:09.535
"No, actually we
need men to work,

00:16:09.535 --> 00:16:11.937
"we need men to be
fathers and husbands,

00:16:11.937 --> 00:16:14.339 align:start size:84% position:16%
"we need men to step
up and provide,"

00:16:14.339 --> 00:16:15.774
we gotta do something different.

00:16:15.774 --> 00:16:17.042
- How much of this
at the end of the day

00:16:17.042 --> 00:16:18.110
do you put on the parents?

00:16:18.110 --> 00:16:19.377
I mean, I think everyone gets

00:16:19.377 --> 00:16:21.413
that the culture's
working against us

00:16:21.413 --> 00:16:24.850
and okay, the movies, the TV
shows, Disney, blah blah blah,

00:16:24.850 --> 00:16:26.051
but at the end of the day,

00:16:26.051 --> 00:16:27.753 align:start size:88% position:13%
and I say this with
certain amount of irony,

00:16:27.753 --> 00:16:30.889 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, I have basically an
8-month-old and a 6-month-old,

00:16:30.889 --> 00:16:32.324
so I'm not there yet.

00:16:32.324 --> 00:16:35.160
But that it really
is you, the parent,

00:16:35.160 --> 00:16:36.595
that should set the agenda here.

00:16:36.595 --> 00:16:37.762
And I think too many parents

00:16:37.762 --> 00:16:39.230 align:start size:84% position:16%
probably just
didn't realize that

00:16:39.230 --> 00:16:42.634
or got lost on their phones
or whatever it might be.

00:16:42.634 --> 00:16:45.303
- Well, I think that it's hard
to parent in this environment

00:16:45.303 --> 00:16:47.272
when it's basically
you versus the world.

00:16:47.272 --> 00:16:48.740
I mean, when it's you

00:16:48.740 --> 00:16:50.242 align:start size:94% position:6%
versus what your kids
are being told in school,

00:16:50.242 --> 00:16:51.844
and what we learned in COVID is,

00:16:51.844 --> 00:16:53.812
and a lot of times parents,

00:16:53.812 --> 00:16:55.047 align:start size:84% position:16%
they don't know what's
going on in school

00:16:55.047 --> 00:16:56.314
not 'cause they
don't wanna know,

00:16:56.314 --> 00:16:57.683
but because as we
found it in COVID,

00:16:57.683 --> 00:16:59.518
administrators keep it from 'em.

00:16:59.518 --> 00:17:00.819 align:start size:81% position:19%
"I wanna see my
kids' curriculum."

00:17:00.819 --> 00:17:02.054
"Oh, no, you're not allowed."

00:17:02.054 --> 00:17:03.655
"No, I wanna come and
sit in on a class."

00:17:03.655 --> 00:17:05.190 align:start size:84% position:16%
"Oh, no, no, you're
not allowed."

00:17:05.190 --> 00:17:06.458 align:start size:84% position:16%
"Oh, I wanna see what
they're reading."

00:17:06.458 --> 00:17:08.493 align:start size:84% position:16%
"No, you're a
domestic terrorist,

00:17:08.493 --> 00:17:10.395
"we're gonna kick you outta
the school board meeting."

00:17:10.395 --> 00:17:12.497
That's what we discovered
in the last couple years.

00:17:12.497 --> 00:17:16.201 align:start position:0%
So parents, whether it's
schools, whether it's big tech,

00:17:16.201 --> 00:17:17.669
I mean the kids
get on the phone,

